Run these scripts as root from the same directory as the compose file, with the postgres container running.

Example backup:

  michael@localhost:~/projects/MyResearch > sudo docker compose up -d
  michael@localhost:~/projects/MyResearch > sudo scripts/pg_dump.sh my_backup
  Dumping to dumps/my_backup.sql
  Success!
  michael@localhost:~/projects/MyResearch > 

You can then wipe your DB using pg_wipe.sh or restore a backup as follows:

  michael@localhost:~/projects/MyResearch > sudo scripts/pg_restore.sh scripts/dumps/my_backup.sql

You will be asked for confirmation before destructive operations. Inspect the scripts for further details.